<p>The United States and Iran will hold a new round of nuclear talks in Geneva on Thursday, with Oman again facilitating and saying there is momentum to “go the extra mile” toward finalising a deal. Iranian President Masoud Pezeshkian and other officials have pointed to “encouraging signals” ahead of the meeting, while Foreign Minister Abbas Araghchi said he expects talks to focus on the details of a possible agreement. He continues to frame diplomacy as the preferred path, even as Iran says it will defend itself if attacked. The talks take place against a sharper military backdrop. Multiple outlets describe a significant US build-up in and around the Middle East, and President Trump has warned limited strikes are possible. Some reporting also says the White House has discussed a targeted strike option that could be followed by a larger attack. With that pressure in the background, Iranian officials have signalled they may accept nuclear concessions if the US lifts sanctions and recognises Iran’s right to “peaceful” enrichment. But the sides still appear to differ on sanctions relief and enrichment. Even so, both countries returning to the table creates a narrow but real opening. For now, negotiators and mediators say their aim going into Thursday is diplomacy, not escalation.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/Kkpzlf4XCWQdd9TDUlN4MwPZZkbcGNH4yobiDotalEcKqkwEoJGubfeSHQ2jDPgwDj5XryOZGpiFCLn4Zyma3l3WH4FNvmH2fNS2ofilu3oD4PvXBzkODABygTcmqFWivH6AbkqRCWyclDGXwX0IKmK-bRTqn4PhBqYGdpIcv9Ztey07K_W6f_kuhYOSbdYjdVbrDlpfaxHgka3D2GaKEE-mXiwOvVGMOytA06lGRTp3BmfNn9M_pNiPUFUnAsP-0Nl_LPIiBH03A1H8Fw' alt='US Navy handout shows the aircraft carrier USS Abraham Lincoln and a guided-missile destroyer sailing in the Arabian Sea, February 6, 2026.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Mediator’s role: Oman cast the Geneva meeting as another (third) Omani-mediated round, underlining Muscat’s continued role as the main channel between Washington and Tehran.</li><li>US envoy remarks: US envoy Steve Witkoff said President Trump is “curious” why Iran has not “capitulated,” a comment that drew wide attention as talks approach.</li><li>Iran’s conditions: A senior Iranian official said Tehran could consider nuclear steps, but described sanctions relief and recognition of enrichment as unresolved. Reporting also points to additional talks planned in early March.</li><li>Domestic backdrop: Some coverage ties the diplomatic push to internal pressure on Iran’s leadership, including renewed protests and broader domestic discontent.</li><li>Force posture: Reporting goes beyond a generic “buildup,” citing satellite imagery that shows a surge in US fighter jets and an “air bridge” of flights into the region, with some calling it the largest deployment since 2003.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Oman (mediator): Oman confirmed the Geneva talks and framed them as the last stretch of diplomacy, saying there is a “positive push” to go further toward finalising a deal. (<a href='https://www.al-monitor.com/originals/2026/02/oman-confirms-us-iran-talks-geneva-thursday'>Al-Monitor</a>)</li><li>Iranian government: Iran says it wants a diplomatic solution but will defend itself; Araghchi said negotiators are drawing up details of a possible deal ahead of the renewed talks. (<a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/iran-vows-to-defend-itself-but-sees-diplomatic-solution-to-us-standoff/article70664604.ece'>The Hindu</a>)</li><li>Iranian leadership: President Masoud Pezeshkian said earlier negotiations have “yielded encouraging signals” ahead of the Geneva round. (<a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/middle-east/trump-curious-why-iran-has-not-capitulated-amid-us-military-buildup-says-witkoff'>The Straits Times</a>)</li><li>US administration: Reporting says President Trump has warned of possible limited strikes and has considered a targeted strike option as leverage while negotiations continue. (<a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/02/22/us/politics/trump-iran-strike-attack.html'>The New York Times</a>)</li><li>Senior Iranian official (via Reuters): Iran signalled it could offer concessions if the US lifts sanctions and recognises Iran’s right to enrich uranium, while noting that differences remain on sanctions relief. (<a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/middle-east/iran-and-us-views-on-sanctions-relief-differ-senior-iranian-official-tells-reuters'>The Straits Times</a>)</li><li>RFE/RL analysis: RFE/RL described Tehran as facing pressure from internal opposition and external threats, which may be shaping its incentives to keep talks going. (<a href='https://www.rferl.org/a/iran-geneva-nuclear-talks-trump-witkoff-protests/33684779.html'>RFE/RL</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.rferl.org/a/iran-geneva-nuclear-talks-trump-witkoff-protests/33684779.html'>Iran, Pressured At Home And Abroad, Looks Set For Third Round Of US Talks</a> - rferl.org</li><li><a href='https://www.pbs.org/newshour/world/u-s-and-iran-to-hold-next-round-of-nuclear-talks-thursday-in-geneva'>U.S. and Iran to hold next round of nuclear talks Thursday in Geneva</a> - pbs.org</li><li><a href='https://www.ndtv.com/world-news/iran-us-talks-expected-thursday-despite-fears-of-strikes-11122555#publisher=newsstand'>Iran-US Talks Expected Thursday Despite Fears Of Strikes</a> - ndtv.com</li><li><a href='https://www.theglobeandmail.com/world/article-iran-us-talks-sanctions-nuclear/'>Iran’s right to ‘peaceful nuclear enrichment’ must be recognized, senior official says</a> - theglobeandmail.com</li><li><a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/02/22/us/politics/trump-iran-strike-attack.html'>Trump Considers Targeted Strike Against Iran, Followed by Larger Attack</a> - nytimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/iran-vows-to-defend-itself-but-sees-diplomatic-solution-to-us-standoff/article70664604.ece'>Iran vows to defend itself but sees diplomatic solution to U.S. standoff</a> - thehindu.com</li><l